<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-AU">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Cookies Policy | Intelligent Talent Matching Platform</title>
    <meta name="description" content="TalentMatch helps candidates find jobs and employers find candidates using intelligent profile and job matching." />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/css/font-awesome.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/css/modern-normalize.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/global.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/policy.css" />
    <script src="/lib/js/jquery.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="<%= theme === 'DARK' ? 'dark-mode' : '' %>">
<%- include('../partials/public-header/public-header'); %>
<main class="policy-page">
    <section class="policy-page__hero" aria-labelledby="cookies-title">
        <div class="policy-page__hero-inner">
            <p class="policy-page__eyebrow">
                Legal
            </p>
            <h1 id="cookies-title" class="policy-page__title">
                Cookie Policy
            </h1>
            <p class="policy-page__intro">
                This Cookie Policy explains how TalentMatch uses cookies and similar
                browser storage technologies to operate the platform, manage sessions,
                remember preferences, and support secure account functionality.
            </p>
            <p class="policy-page__updated">
                Last updated: 31 May 2026
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="policy-page__layout" aria-label="Cookie policy content">
        <aside class="policy-page__sidebar" aria-label="Cookie policy sections">
            <nav class="policy-page__nav">
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#overview">Overview</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#what-cookies-are">What cookies are</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#cookies-we-use">Cookies we use</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#session-cookies">Session cookies</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#preference-cookies">Preference cookies</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#security-cookies">Security cookies</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#third-party-cookies">Third-party cookies</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#managing-cookies">Managing cookies</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#changes">Changes</a>
                <a class="policy-page__nav-link" href="#contact">Contact</a>
            </nav>
        </aside>
        <article class="policy-page__content">
            <section id="overview" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 1. Overview </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch uses cookies and related browser storage technologies to provide core platform functionality, maintain user sessions, remember preferences, and support account security. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> This Cookie Policy should be read together with our <a class="policy-page__inline-link" href="/privacy"> Privacy Policy </a>, which explains how personal information is collected, used, stored, and protected. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="what-cookies-are" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 2. What Cookies Are </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Cookies are small text files placed on your device by a website or web application. They allow the platform to recognise your browser, maintain session state, remember preferences, and provide a consistent user experience. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Similar technologies may include server-side sessions, local storage, session storage, and browser-based identifiers used to support platform functionality. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="cookies-we-use" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 3. Cookies We Use </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch may use the following types of cookies and storage technologies: </p>
                <ul class="policy-page__list">
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Essential cookies required for login, sessions, account access, and secure platform use.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Preference cookies used to remember settings such as light mode or dark mode.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Security cookies used to help protect accounts, sessions, and platform workflows.</li>
                    <li class="policy-page__list-item">Functional storage used to support user interface behaviour and improve usability.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
            <section id="session-cookies" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 4. Session Cookies </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch uses session cookies to keep users signed in and connect browser requests to a secure server-side session. These cookies help the platform identify whether a user is authenticated and maintain account workflows. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Session cookies may include a session identifier. The session data itself is stored on the server where possible, rather than exposing account details directly in the browser. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="preference-cookies" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 5. Preference Cookies </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch may remember basic user preferences, including theme selection such as light mode or dark mode. This helps provide a consistent experience across pages and visits. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> If you are signed in, some preferences may also be stored with your account so they can be restored when you use the platform on another device. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="security-cookies" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 6. Security Cookies </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Cookies and sessions may be used to support security measures such as authentication, session expiry, activity tracking, protection against unauthorised access, and prevention of misuse. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> These cookies are considered essential because disabling them may prevent the platform from functioning correctly or securely. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="third-party-cookies" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 7. Third-Party Cookies </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch is not intended to use third-party advertising cookies as part of its core recruitment functionality. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Some external resources, such as fonts, icons, libraries, or embedded services, may be loaded from third-party providers depending on the platform configuration. Those providers may apply their own cookie or privacy practices. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="managing-cookies" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 8. Managing Cookies </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> You can manage or disable cookies through your browser settings. Most browsers allow you to block cookies, delete existing cookies, or receive alerts when cookies are being used. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> If you disable essential cookies, some TalentMatch features may not work correctly, including login, account access, saved preferences, applications, recommendations, and secure session-based workflows. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="changes" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 9. Changes to This Cookie Policy </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> TalentMatch may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in platform functionality, security practices, technology, or legal requirements. </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Continued use of the platform after updates are published constitutes acknowledgement of the updated Cookie Policy. </p>
            </section>
            <section id="contact" class="policy-page__section">
                <h2 class="policy-page__section-title"> 10. Contact </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> Questions about this Cookie Policy may be directed to: </p>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph"> <a class="policy-page__inline-link" href="mailto:support@talentmatch.com"> support@talentmatch.com </a> </p>
            </section>
            <section class="policy-page__note" aria-label="Important note">
                <h2 class="policy-page__note-title">
                    Academic Project Disclaimer
                </h2>
                <p class="policy-page__paragraph">
                    TalentMatch and all associated policies, terms, and documentation have been
                    developed as part of CSIT314 – Systems Development Methodologies at the
                    University of Wollongong for academic assessment purposes. These documents
                    have not been reviewed by legal professionals and are not intended to
                    constitute legal advice or create legally binding obligations. Any future
                    production or commercial deployment should be subject to independent legal,
                    privacy, and regulatory review.
                </p>
            </section>
        </article>
    </section>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/footer/footer'); %>
<script src="/js/global.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
